From ea4b41083d82e1d8abf11adf4047a367306a618d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 22:02:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02684/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md;
 verifier_is_oracle=false) -- Config-rule VOCABULARY transfer from
 previously-seen games (the operator's 'derive config-rules from
 previously-seen games' direction). .407's self-learning line is dead: the
 localizer-compounding axis saturated (exp4407 F1=1.0 flat) because the
 position-bound localizer had no headroom. The NEW substrate WITH real
 headroom: the 9 toggle/config games and their GROUNDED win-rules. THE STEP:
 build a config-rule VOCABULARY of RELATIONAL primitives (count-equality,
 position-match, glyph-map, symmetry, region-match, ...) extracted from the
 GROUNDED win-rules of solved config games (ka59
 editable-count==reference-count; tr87 glyph-rewrite; tn36 program-editor;
 sc25 cast-grid; + any new exp4414 groundings), then measure whether SEEDING
 the scaffolded inducer with the vocabulary (offer the primitives as candidate
 relation templates) raises the win-rule GROUNDING rate on HELD-OUT config
 games vs COLD-START (no vocabulary). Emit config_rule_vocabulary_transfers
 BARE bool := (the vocabulary-seeded grounding rate EXCEEDS the cold-start
 grounding rate on held-out config games, delta CI95-excl-0, with a
 leave-one-game-out control). verifier_is_oracle=false (the transfer object is
 a learned config-rule vocabulary; grounding is execution but the COMPOUNDING
 claim is about the learned vocabulary). A win = the verifier-grounded
 config-rule program COMPOUNDS via transfer (the self-learning headline on the
 axis that now has real headroom); a clean null (the vocabulary does not
 transfer -- config-game win-rules are too heterogeneous) is decision-grade
 (the registry already refuted GENERIC-grid-feature cross-game transfer for
 the NAV hard tail; this tests RELATIONAL config-rule vocabulary, a different
 object). Cached/local; the inducer is the local gemma-12B on the iGPU; zero
 quota; NO TRM training. NOT gated.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
